{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates","id":1057671,"title":"Help with Custom Legacy built around the Three Fates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-03T11:25:39-08:00","id":1057671,"title":"Help with Custom Legacy built around the Three Fates","content":"Trying to build a Legacy around the Three Sisters Fate from Greek Mythology but I don't know that much about them and could use some help. I was looking at Fate and Time as the Ruling and Optional Arcanum, They would be Acanthus and probably Mysterium. What I have for attainments I am not sure if they fit the theme.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Thread Cutters </span></span></b><br /> Thread Cutters, or Euthanist as they are sometimes called, are the enforcers of Fate and the guides of Destiny. Everyman, Institution, and Government has a \u201cTrue Purpose\u201d to fulfil and it is the duty of the Thread Cutters to ensure that it does so \u2013 but only as long as Fate decrees that they should exist. Thread Cutters define this as the ability of the subject to do his, her or its duty without causing undue harm. The Legacy has a reputation for solving problems with torture and assassination, but the truth of the matter is that most of the Thread Cutters\u2019 work is nonviolent. Destroying a decrepit corporation through bankruptcy is easier than killing.<br /> <br /> The Euthanist has many duties and most of them are joyous and wonderful, some not so pleasant yet necessary. The Beginning is a time for growth and prosperity, encouraging this grow by promoting good fortune is one of the joys of their duties. Then the person or institution enters the Being stage at which they realize their true purpose. It is at this stage that the Euthanist watches and ensures that this true purpose is followed harmoniously and without harm to others. Then there is the Ending, all people and institution have a defined ending and this is also enforced. To exist after the end is disruptive and harmful to all other destinies and therefore must not be allowed.<br /> <br /> To ensure that the ending is adhered to the Euthanist will use every tool at their disposal to bring about that ending. The end of one\u2019s true purpose does not denote that they have lived a long and prosperous life. Sometimes even a child has reached its end before it has reached puberty. The ending is marked by the one fulfilling its true purpose or when their continued existence brings harm to others. To this end the Euthanist will terminate anything that has reached its Ending and yet still exists, the Tremere being at the top of this list.<br /> <br /> Because of their duties to bring about the end they are not always viewed in the best of lights. There are those within the mage society that look at what they do with distain and say that they carry their duties to far. Yet there are those that claim they are a \u201cNecessary Evil\u201d and that the Euthanist are just weeding out the bad apples. The Euthanist will follow the Lex Magica as long as it suites their purpose and for that they are shunned. Thread Cutters must remain a hidden society within a hidden society.<br /> <br /> For a complete understanding of the Thread Cutters and their duties please see \u201cLegacies: the Ancient\u201d page 100.<br /> <br /> <b>History:</b> The Thread Cutters are a truly ancient Legacy. Initiates contemplate the paradox of a Legacy that is obsessed with impermanence, yet has survived, continuously, for at least 7,000 years. Euthanist parameters say that the Thread Cutters renew themselves by adapting to their environment. They have introduced the Three into many different culture and allow that culture to perceive them as they will.<br /> <br /> For a complete Historical account of the Thread Cutters please see \u201cLegacies: the Ancient\u201d page 102.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Origins </span></span></b><br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Acanthus or Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Euthanist<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Euthanist normally try to remain inconspicuous in their dress and manners. To call attention to one\u2019s self is to invite scrutiny and that would lead to being discovered. Being discovered would not allow them to complete their duties, so we must remain inconspicuous. The Surreptitious use of their powers is also part of their blending.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Doctrine </span></span></b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Fate 2, Empathy 2, Investigation 2, and either Intimidation 2 or Persuasion 2<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Euthanist seek out their initiates early grooming them for the hard road ahead. They look for those that have a marked destiny as one of their numbers or for those that have a predisposition for seeing what must be done. They will tutor them and in their ways and in their special use of the Fate Arcanum until they are ready, this is called the beginning. Then when they are ready to be inducted into the Legacy the will undergo the initiation ritual. Full initiation entails a form of temporary death called the Agama (\u201crevelation\u201d). This is a rote that suspends the target\u2019s life and plunges her soul into the Underworld. Bound to a ghostly form, she searches for the lost path to Stygia.<br /> <br /> Mages that come to this calling later in their careers to not need to go through the tutoring portion of the training but must still complete the Agama to become a full member of this Legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> The Euthanist are meet on occasion to share stories and ideas and to keep in touch with each other. This is also where they will call attention to any matter that they feel they should work on as a group, a truly scary proposition. They have, on occasion, been called together to bring charges against one of their own. There are few things that they consider a crime worthy of calling for a trial. One is to charge a member with interference in another Euthanist duties. Another is for allowing someone to escape their destiny by not performing the Ending. They can also be charged with the worst crime of all, changing their own destiny to avoid their Ending.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Magic </span></span></b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Fate<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Shears/Scissors +1 tool; Spool of thread +1 tool; Casting the Bones +1 tool; Viewing the subjects destiny +2 Sympathetic; Flipping a Coin +1 tool.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Presiding over or attending funerals; Self-mutilation; Casting lots; Meditating near a corpse; Painting the image of a skeleton or the Three; Burning flowers; Traditional mourning (wailing and tearing clothes in some cultures); Fasting; One hour of walking while blindfolded.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Attainments </span></span></b><br /> The attainment of the Euthanists always revolve around Fate, be it the Beginning, the being, or the Ending. For this reason their main Arcanum is Fate. Since one of their main tenants is to ensure that nothing outlives it Destiny and True Purpose they are expected to deliver the Ending, so Death is a natural Optional Arcanum. Unless stated in the attainment none of these attainments can benefit the Euthanists. The Thread Cutter society takes a bid view of a Euthanists that would use these attainments outside of the discharge of their duties. With that in mind the Euthanists had better be certain that the subject is in violation of their Destiny before punishment or on the correct path before rewarding them. To do otherwise could bring them under the scrutiny of their fellow Euthanists.<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b> Scrutinize Fate.<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Fate 2.<br /> This attainment is a specialized form of the \u201cInterconnections\u201d spell that allows the Euthanist to determine if there is an outside force directing the subject\u2019s destiny. Instead of the ability to view the sympathetic connection with the people, places, or things around the subject the Euthanists is able to view if the subject is being possessed, mind controlled, or if his destiny has been altered by an external force. This is difficult at first but as the Euthanists advances in the Fate Arcanum it becomes easier to accomplish to a point where it becomes second nature. Each activation of this attainment is an instant action. It is Withstood by the subject\u2019s Composure. (Reach: Instant Casting).<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 2<br /> If the Euthanists also has Death 2 he is able to take a momentary look at the subject\u2019s soul. This slows them to determine the health of their soul and glean specific information about the subject. This is a specialized form of the \u201cSoul Mark\u201d spell that specifically looks for evidence that of Soul Tampering, if they have Consumed a Soul or if the subject is under a Persistent Conditions that prevent the subject from fulfilling their destiny. As with the main ability of this attainment it is difficult at first but gets easier with time. Each activation of this attainment is an instant action. It is Withstood by the subject\u2019s Resolve. (Reach: Instant Casting).<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Fate 2.<br /> This attainment allows them to help others stay on the path that they are destined for. When looking at a subject they first determine if they are on track with their Destiny and if they are not what steps are needed to get them back on track. This is a specialized form of the \u201cSerendipity\u201d spell where her stated goal is to help their target stay the course. Each activation of this attainment is an instantaneous action that lasts for up to 1 week. (Reaches: Instant Casting, Advanced Duration).<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 2<br /> This particular curse is one of the more effective things a Euthanists can do to a subject to get them to repent their ways and to return to their path of destiny. This is mainly used on murders so that they can hear the voices of their victims and be haunted by what they have done. It can be used on other to hear the voices of their lost loved ones professing a deep shame for the path that they are on. The Euthanists cannot control what the dead say or that they would say anything at all, but could use other methods to secure the ghost\u2019s cooperation. This is a specialized version of the \u201cSpeak with the Dead\u201d spell. Each casting of this spell takes an instant action and the hauntings can last up to a year (starting at a day for Death 2 and advancing to a Year at Death 5). (Reaches: Instant Casting, Advanced Duration).<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 4, Fate 3, Empathy 3.<br /> This attainment is used as a reward and a punishment. For the subject this could be a boon or a hex depending on the circumstances for which it was used. If the subject is true to his destiny then he receives a boon and good luck will follow, for the subject that has strayed from the path this is a hex. This is a specialized use of the \u201cExceptional Luck\u201d spell.<br /> In game terms if the subject receives a boon the subject receives a bonus equal to the Euthanists Fate, this will affect a number of rolls equal to the Euthanists Fate, chosen by the subject. If the subject receives a Hex then he receives a negative equal to the Euthanists Fate, this will affect the next rolls equal to the Euthanists Fate. Each casting of this attainment is an instant action and it can last for up to a week. This is Withstood by Composure. (Reaches: Instant Casting, Advanced Duration).<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 3<br /> In order to protect a subject from someone that would use soul magic to veer then from their destiny the Euthanists can use the \u201cSoul Armor\u201d spell on the subject. This is an instant action and can last up to a year at the higher levels of Fate. (Reaches: Instant Casting, Advanced Duration).<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6, Fate 4.<br /> This attainment can bind up to two parties into an oath. This is effectively the same as the \u201cSworn Oath\u201d spell. A subject that has sworn an oath in this manner is magically compelled to keep that oath. As long as he abides by the terms he will be granted a Boon (as per Boon on page 134) and if he violates the oath then he will suffer the effects of the hex that was agreed upon when the oath was given. Each casting of this attainment takes an instant action and lasts for up to a year. (Reaches: Instant Casting, Advanced Duration, Up to two people).<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 4<br /> A Euthanists with Death 4 gains the effects of a \u201cWithering\u201d spell. This spell is the one that has given the Euthanists their reputation as assassins and is one of their most fears attainments. This spell is used as pure punishment and a single touch does lethal damage equal to the Euthanists Death rating. (Reach: Instant Casting).<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 8, Fate 5.<br /> This attainment is used as a curse so that the subject will suffer the harm that he visits upon others. If he stabs someone he will feel the pain and receive a stab wound in the same spot. No matter what harm he does to another it will befall him as well, and if that harm results in death he too will die. This is a specialized casting of the \u201cShared Fate\u201d spell. Each casting of the spell is a ritual casting and lasts for up to a week. It is Withstood by Composure. (Reaches: Advanced Duration, +2 special)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 5<br /> This attainment has two main purposes. The first is to remove a person from the annals of history and the second is to carry out an assassination. A Euthanists can erase someone from the world, removing any evidence that they even existed. This is done to the cruelest of subject those whose very name inspires others to do harm. This is similar to the effect of the \u201cEmpty Presence\u201d spell and usually proceeds an assassination.<br /> The other use is on the Euthanists himself and is used to get close to someone and assassinate them. This turns him invisible, as per the spell, and allowing him to get close enough to the subject to assassinate him. The real sinister part of this spell is that it also removes any forewarning that mage was has marked the subject for assassination, as there is no evidence that the mage existed. This is the one attainment, in this Legacy, that the Euthanists can use upon himself.<br /> Each casting of this attainment uses an instant action and 1 mana, it lasts for up to 1 year. It is Withstood by Composure. (Reach: Instant Casting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-06-2017, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T11:52:42-08:00","id":1057689,"title":"","content":"The attainments are probably fine, hard to say if they fit the theme though since just The Fates is pretty barebones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T14:25:10-08:00","id":1057765,"title":"","content":"If you need a point of reference, Thread Cutters from &quot;Legacies: the Ancient&quot; are what you describe. Their Arcana are Fate and Death. While their fluff is worth a read, their Attainments need some reworking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:03:52-08:00","id":1057774,"title":"","content":"Ok I will will look them up, the Death Arcanum is not what I wanted but than may be replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:29:25-08:00","id":1057786,"title":"","content":"The Thread-Cutters use Death, because they're actually based on the Euthanatos/Chakravanti Tradition from Mage: The Ascension (or at least, the real-life philosophy and mythos that partly inspired them). <br /> <br /> Connecting them to the Greek Moirae, they'd be disciples of Atropos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:37:34-08:00","id":1057788,"title":"","content":"I just read the Legacy in the Book and the Three are definitely the base of the Three fates for legend and Lore. Now I need to try an convert them to the 2e version. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> If you could help that would be appreciated. You seen to have a good head for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:21:50-08:00","id":1057816,"title":"","content":"Let's see... they teach that death is a sad but natural, inevitable, and ultimately necessary part of life. So they're here to make all those deaths meaningful and worthy, helping people die the Good Death. Through this they help turn the Wheel of Ages so that it does not break. <br /> <br /> I'd say they indeed are an Acanthus Legacy, what with the focus on destiny, choice, and consequence. Death is their Ruling Arcanum, helping them both detect those who defy deah and bring death to them. Fate is their optional Arcanum, used to bless those brave and resolute in the face of death and curse those who would cower. I'm not with my laptop now, so I can't come up with good Attainments at this moment. <br /> <br /> And it just occurred to me that I basically described a cult of assassins who go after Liches up there. That's the direction I'd take them, should I be converting/remaking them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:43:13-08:00","id":1057829,"title":"","content":"That all sounds great, I will look at attainments and see if we come up with the same stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:17:50-08:00","id":1057878,"title":"","content":"Just to throw some history of Mage into the mix, the realm of Arcadia used to look a whole lot more Greek until Merlin came along. Perhaps this legacy exists as some kind of remnant shard of the previous iteration of the Acanthus path? If so have they quietly accepted the changes made to their Path or are they trying some scheme or following some agenda to restore it to what it was? If so, how have they managed to cling to their original Supernal identity? Mind you, Merlin's changes did spit in the Ruin's face, but he was such an asshole about it how he got it done...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:29:42-08:00","id":1057884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057878#post1057878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to throw some history of Mage into the mix, the realm of Arcadia used to look a whole lot more Greek until Merlin came along. Perhaps this legacy exists as some kind of remnant shard of the previous iteration of the Acanthus path? If so have they quietly accepted the changes made to their Path or are they trying some scheme or following some agenda to restore it to what it was? If so, how have they managed to cling to their original Supernal identity? Mind you, Merlin's changes did spit in the Ruin's face, but he was such an asshole about it how he got it done...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also good material, especially if the Legacy focuses on the Greek Fates instead of the Norse Norn or the Hindu Trimurti.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T01:31:54-08:00","id":1057969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057878#post1057878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to throw some history of Mage into the mix, the realm of Arcadia used to look a whole lot more Greek until Merlin came along. Perhaps this legacy exists as some kind of remnant shard of the previous iteration of the Acanthus path? If so have they quietly accepted the changes made to their Path or are they trying some scheme or following some agenda to restore it to what it was? If so, how have they managed to cling to their original Supernal identity? Mind you, Merlin's changes did spit in the Ruin's face, but he was such an asshole about it how he got it done...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure what this means, What changed in the Path? Remember I am relatively new to Mage the Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T01:42:35-08:00","id":1057970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057969#post1057969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not sure what this means, What changed in the Path? Remember I am relatively new to Mage the Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how the Path of Thorns (and by extension the concept of destiny, chance, fortune, luck, etc) is associated with fairies nowadays? Specifically, the kinds inspired by the Celtic and related gods?<br /> <br /> That only happened as a side-effect of Merlin's Ascension, who in MtAw was an archmaster of the now non-existant kingdom of Camelot. Until then, the primary Path symbolism of the Acanthus were the various gods of fate. However, since Supernal actions retroactively edit reality, the Path symbolism of the Acanthus has now always been the Fair Folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T02:13:49-08:00","id":1057973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057970#post1057970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know how the Path of Thorns (and by extension the concept of destiny, chance, fortune, luck, etc) is associated with fairies nowadays? Specifically, the kinds inspired by the Celtic and related gods?<br /> <br /> That only happened as a side-effect of Merlin's Ascension, who in MtAw was an archmaster of the now non-existant kingdom of Camelot. Until then, the primary Path symbolism of the Acanthus were the various gods of fate. However, since Supernal actions retroactively edit reality, the Path symbolism of the Acanthus has now always been the Fair Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I wasn't aware of any of that and I would say that they are clinging to the Past and trying to change it back. They would probably feel that the are destined to return the Path to what it once was, restoring the Three to their former glory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacies of the Ancient, pg. 101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faces of the Three<br /> Thread Cutters almost always identify the Three with existing gods and goddesses. Thread Cutter magic invokes these deities (and their attendant rites and symbols) according to particular magical associations. A Euthanist might channel Clotho (Beginning) to \u201cweave\u201d wounded flesh to heal with Life magic, or call upon Kali (Ending) to master Death. The Fate Arcanum is fundamental to the Three, so a Euthanist may cast Fate spells while invoking any of them. Legacy mages do not always agree on specific occult associations, but those listed below are the most widely accepted.<br /> <b>Beginning:</b> Clotho of the Fates, Tisiphone of the Furies and Urd of the Norns; Nemain of the Celts (especially for frenzied or violent creation) and the Indian deities Sarasvati and Brahma. Beginning is also associated with the <span style=\"color:blue\">Life, Prime and Spirit Arcana as well as the Shadow Realm.</span><br /> <b>Being:</b> Lachesis of the Fates, Megaera of the Furies and Verdandi of the Norns; Anann of the Celts and the Indian deities Lahkshmi and Vishnu. Being is also associated with the <span style=\"color:blue\">Mind, Forces and Space Arcana as well as the Astral Plane.</span><br /> <b>Ending:</b> Atropos of the Fates, Alecto of the Furies and Skuld of the Norns; Morrigan of the Celts and the Indian deities Shiva and Durga (particularly as Kali). Ending is also associated with the <span style=\"color:blue\">Death, Matter and Time Arcana as well as the Underworld.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>What I don't understand about the thread cutters is the above, does that mean that there are 3 versions of the Legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T03:10:16-08:00","id":1057980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057973#post1057973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't understand about the thread cutters is the above, does that mean that there are 3 versions of the Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>can</i> be, but in 2nd Ed terms this piece of text describes their Yantras. Even a Fate/Death Thread Cutter may want to summon rain with Forces. When they do, they invoke Lachesis in their casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T03:45:45-08:00","id":1057984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057878#post1057878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to throw some history of Mage into the mix, the realm of Arcadia used to look a whole lot more Greek until Merlin came along. Perhaps this legacy exists as some kind of remnant shard of the previous iteration of the Acanthus path? If so have they quietly accepted the changes made to their Path or are they trying some scheme or following some agenda to restore it to what it was? If so, how have they managed to cling to their original Supernal identity? Mind you, Merlin's changes did spit in the Ruin's face, but he was such an asshole about it how he got it done...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually now that I read more of the Legacy, if it was changed then it was destined to change and the death of the old Arcadia was its ending. The Arcadia that Merlin brought about was the Beginning of the New Arcadia. If they feel that the usurper prematurely ended the Old Arcadia then they may be looking end this iteration and start anew. But the end of the old, prematurely or not, is still the end.<br /> <br /> What do you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T03:46:40-08:00","id":1057985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057980#post1057980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>can</i> be, but in 2nd Ed terms this piece of text describes their Yantras. Even a Fate/Death Thread Cutter may want to summon rain with Forces. When they do, they invoke Lachesis in their casting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure I get how that defines their Yantras but I see where you are going with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T03:54:24-08:00","id":1057987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057984#post1057984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually now that I read more of the Legacy, if it was changed then it was destined to change and the death of the old Arcadia was its ending. The Arcadia that Merlin brought about was the Beginning of the New Arcadia. If they feel that the usurper prematurely ended the Old Arcadia then they may be looking end this iteration and start anew. But the end of the old, prematurely or not, is still the end.<br /> <br /> What do you think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly legit. The Three are the Three, no matter what mask they wear.<br /> <br /> And I also agree with Teatime on invoking the various gods that the Three manifest as as Yantras. Because I can totally see one of these guys holding a <i>lingam </i>to invoke Shiva and cast a Death spell, or a long hand-woven scarf to invoke Lachesis and cast a Forces spell, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T04:04:09-08:00","id":1057988,"title":"","content":"What do you think about this<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Attainments </span></span></b><br /> The attainments of the Euthanists always revolve around Fate, be it the Beginning, the Being, or the Ending. For this reason their main Arcanum is Fate. Since they are infamous with the methods of their endings they are more closely related to Death as an Optional Arcanum, however some choose to substitute their own Parxis for the Death option.<br /> <br /> I feel this because above all they serve Fate, all forms of Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T04:07:48-08:00","id":1057989,"title":"","content":"Not sure what you meant by substituting Praxes for Death. Do you mean they can have Arcana other than Death as their Optional Arcanum in their Attainments? If so, are all Arcana available for the choice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T04:16:07-08:00","id":1057991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057989#post1057989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what you meant by substituting Praxes for Death. Do you mean they can have Arcana other than Death as their Optional Arcanum in their Attainments? If so, are all Arcana available for the choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and Life for the Beginning, Mind for the Being, and Death as the Ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T04:20:22-08:00","id":1057993,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it feels more like three Legacies working under a shared paradigm. Do you then have ideas for those Attainments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T04:24:08-08:00","id":1057994,"title":"","content":"Not yet but I have added some to the Attainment section<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Attainments </span></span></b><br /> The attainment of the Euthanists always revolve around Fate, be it the Beginning, the being, or the Ending. For this reason their main Arcanum is Fate. Since they are infamous with the methods of their endings they are more closely related to Death as an Optional Arcanum, however some choose to substitute their own Parxis for the Death option. The Optional Arcanum is limited to Life for the Beginning, Mind for the Being, and Death for the Ending. This Substitution would require that the Attainment be purchased as an Untutored Legacy Attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T05:19:22-08:00","id":1058002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057973#post1057973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't understand about the thread cutters is the above, does that mean that there are 3 versions of the Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>No there's only one version of the legacy, but they classify their symbolic associations according to the taxonomy and purpose of the Fates. Basically, the Pentacle is agnostic-ish, it sees the ten arcana and their purposes as each being separate, the Thread Cutters are deistic and acknowledge the difference between them, but they also organize them in clusters attached in purpose to one or the three Fates. The text you're quoting is talking about their symbolic associations for casting magic, not about being in three different legacies. Note that each of those clusters is 4 arcana which is at least one arcana too many to start basing attainments on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T05:31:06-08:00","id":1058005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058002#post1058002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that each of those clusters is 4 arcana which is at least one arcana too many to start basing attainments on.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? I am totally lost by this statement. Each had 3 Arcana and they all shared Fate. And where does it state that you can build and attainment on only three Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T05:45:52-08:00","id":1058009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058005#post1058005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? I am totally lost by this statement. Each had 3 Arcana and they all shared Fate. And where does it state that you can build and attainment on only three Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mispoke, you can only use two arcana for legacy attainments not 3 (I was getting the fact that a member of a legacy usually has a default of 3 ruling arcana to their name confused with the number of arcana in attainments). Since each Fate has a cluster of 4 arcana under it (Fate being one of them in all cases) you'd need 3 legacies for each Fate instead of just one. For instance with Beginning you'd need a Fate/Life, Fate/Prime and Fate/Spirit set of legacies.<br /> <br /> Still the point stands, what you're looking at is a division of magic symbolism and clusters of arcana purpose under each Fate, not a division of the Thread Cutters into separate legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T05:59:59-08:00","id":1058013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058009#post1058009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mispoke, you can only use two arcana for legacy attainments not 3 (I was getting the fact that a member of a legacy usually has a default of 3 ruling arcana to their name confused with the number of arcana in attainments). Since each Fate has a cluster of 4 arcana under it (Fate being one of them in all cases) you'd need 3 legacies for each Fate instead of just one. For instance with Beginning you'd need a Fate/Life, Fate/Prime and Fate/Spirit set of legacies.<br /> <br /> Still the point stands, what you're looking at is a division of magic symbolism and clusters of arcana purpose under each Fate, not a division of the Thread Cutters into separate legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok that makes sense, I am fine with leaving them as Fate Prime and Death as Optional. I just feel that Ending is getting more attention than the other two and they are all three just as important to the Thread Cutters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-04-2017, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T06:08:22-08:00","id":1058014,"title":"","content":"Well, that is the purpose of the Thread Cutters specifically, so I'll grant you that they are getting the heaviest focus. I also don't see a problem with an association of legacies that adhere to the same symbols as the Thread Cutters but go off in different directions or focus on different Fates. I was just clarifying what that paragraph you were quoting was about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T06:55:40-08:00","id":1058022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1057993#post1057993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it feels more like three Legacies working under a shared paradigm. Do you then have ideas for those Attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am thinking about these as the Attainments, Comments, suggestions, replacements?<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> Quantum Flux (Fate \u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> Interconnections (Fate \u2022)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b><br /> Soul Marks (Death \u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> Exceptional Luck (Fate \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b><br /> Suppress Aura (Death \u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> Warding Gesture (Fate \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b><br /> Soul Armor (Death \u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> Shared Fate (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b><br /> Sever Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T07:08:17-08:00","id":1058027,"title":"","content":"I'd make a direct damage spell a part of the attainments, thus it's not a Wisdom sin to slay someone in the name of the Fates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T10:25:23-08:00","id":1058076,"title":"","content":"Don't use &quot;Sever Soul&quot; as an Attainment. Thread Cutters are all about maintaining the reincarnation cycle. Removing Souls out of it would be a greater blasphemy for them, than even for mainstream Orders. Injuring Spells are fine, though. The fifth Attainment could allow you to kill Instantly with a touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T10:43:49-08:00","id":1058091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058076#post1058076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't use &quot;Sever Soul&quot; as an Attainment. Thread Cutters are all about maintaining the reincarnation cycle. Removing Souls out of it would be a greater blasphemy for them, than even for mainstream Orders. Injuring Spells are fine, though. The fifth Attainment could allow you to kill Instantly with a touch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconding this unless they had another attainment that allowed them to &quot;purify&quot; and then release it to the Diamond Wheel or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:25:13-08:00","id":1058111,"title":"","content":"I had some time to think about Fate Attainments. Here we go:<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Quantum Flux .(Fate \u2022, +1R Instant casting)<br /> It's a useful Attainment, but it doesn't resonate with Thread Cutter's philosophy all that much.<br /> <br /> Serendipity (Fate \u2022, +1R Instant casting)<br /> It would provide knowledge how to repair subject's Dharma. Useful and resonant with the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Automatic Successes on Active Mage Sight for a single Arcanum<br /> Number of successes is equal to number of dots of the Relevant Arcanum. In this case it's Fate or Death. The sample Legacy in the Corebook has this as the first optional Attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Interconnections (Fate \u2022, +2R special effect)<br /> I suggest modifying it for your use. With some changes, it could emulate the first Attainment from &quot;Legacies: the Ancient&quot;. The casting time lasts a Scene, but if the Attainment only measures karma, that makes it limited compared to the base Spell. You could consider making it Instant.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Exceptional Luck (Fate \u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R Duration)<br /> It's a great and versatile Spell that can be used both for punishment and reward. Other effects, like &quot;Grave Misfortune&quot; are also appropriate, but are limited to curses.<br /> <br /> Warding Gesture (Fate \u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R Duration)<br /> Good for protecting the subject's destiny, but only from outside tampering. Thread Cutters with this Attainment expect getting into a fight with other powerful entities. As such, it's not for everybody.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Sworn Oaths (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R Duration)<br /> One way of keeping their subject on the right track. This Attainment requires the Mage to make themselves known. As such, it's not for everybody.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Shared Fate (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Duration OR Instant Casting, +2R special effect)<br /> Very thematic as a tool of poetic justice. Sort of reminds me of the Ghost Attainment from &quot;Legacies: the Ancient&quot;. However, It needs a lot of Reach to be useful.<br /> <br /> Divine Intervention OR Strings of Fate (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R Duration)<br /> Like Sworn Oaths, only more powerful. You might want to play with Reach if you want to make it a fourth Attainment. However, it makes Sworn Oaths slightly redundant.<br /> <br /> Pariah (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Duration)<br /> Tricky to cast, but powerful in it's own right. Useful when you want to isolate the target from society, without killing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T13:25:10-08:00","id":1058126,"title":"","content":"And now Death Attainments:<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Soul Marks .(Death \u2022, +1R Instant casting)<br /> A nifty source of information that's resonant with the Legacy. Thread Cutters need to judge a Soul before they determine its fate.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Decay (Death \u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting)<br /> Only slightly resonant with the Legacy, but versatile and useful.<br /> <br /> Soul Armor (Death \u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting OR Duration)<br /> Guiding a Soul to its end requires protecting it. When cast Ritually it can protect multiple people. When cast Instantly it's only good for the Thread Cutter - you might consider making it permanent.<br /> <br /> Speak with the Dead (Death \u2022, +1R Instant casting, +1R Duration)<br /> Used as a curse it can drive killers mad with voices of their victims, or push others to make amends for their misdeeds.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Decay (Death \u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R special effect)<br /> As above, only more powerful.<br /> <br /> Ghost Gate (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting)<br /> Push the target through the portal. Let them out after a few hours. They will be naked and sorry for everything. It's also good for spying.<br /> <br /> Soul Armor (Death \u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R Duration)<br /> As above, only better for protecting others.<br /> <br /> Touch of the Grave (Death \u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R Duration)<br /> Like &quot;Speak with the Dead&quot;, only now Ghosts can punch them.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Ghost Gate (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R special effect)<br /> As above, only you don't need to wrestle with your targets. Also, everyone keeps their clothes.<br /> <br /> Withering (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting)<br /> Deal Lethal Damage to your victims without suffering Wisdom loss.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Withering (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting, +1R Sensory OR Aggravated)<br /> Deal Lethal (possibly Aggravated) Damage to your victims without suffering Wisdom loss.<br /> <br /> ??? (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, +1R Instant Casting)<br /> At this point you can kill with a touch. If you beat their Withstand rating and they're not otherwise protected, they die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T13:30:29-08:00","id":1058130,"title":"","content":"Empty Presence is kind of one of the ultimate assassin powers. I think you'd want it to be Instant Activation, then you could ambush someone, use the attainment again and then ambush them again if that's even necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:52:52-08:00","id":1058183,"title":"","content":"Ok this is what I have so far<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:19px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Attainments </span></span></b><br /> The attainment of the Euthanists always revolve around Fate, be it the Beginning, the being, or the Ending. For this reason their main Arcanum is Fate. Since they are infamous with the methods of their endings they are more closely related to Death as an Optional Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Fate 2, Empathy<br /> Serendipity (Fate \u2022, Instant Cast, 2 Turn Duration, Potency = Fate)<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Fate 2<br /> Interconnections (Fate \u2022, Instant Cast, +1 Special, 2 Turn Duration, Potency = Fate)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 2<br /> Soul Marks (Death \u2022, Instant Cast, +1 Free Soul Special, 2 Turn Duration, Potency = Death)<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 4, Fate 3<br /> Exceptional Luck (Fate \u2022\u2022, Instant Cast, Advanced Duration, 1 Day duration, Potency = Fate)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 3<br /> Rotting Flesh (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Instant Cast, 2 Turn Duration, Potency = Death)<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6, Fate 4<br /> Sworn Oaths (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022, Instant Cast, Advanced Duration, 1 month duration, Potency = 1)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 4<br /> Devouring the Slain (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Instant Cast, Not Injured Special, 3 turn Duration, Potency = Death)<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 8, Fate 5<br /> Shared Fate (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022, Instant Cast, Advanced Duration, +1 Special, 1 week Duration, Potency = Fate)<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Death 5<br /> Withering (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Instant Cast, Aggravated Damage, 3 Turn Duration, Potency = Death)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-04-2017, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:25:58-08:00","id":1058208,"title":"","content":"They have both Rotting Flesh and Withering as Attainments? While that sounds like overkill, I can't really judge when I don't know under what chain of logic you followed to build them. The overall function of the Attainments look like &quot;punish the target for stepping out of dharma&quot; - am I correct?<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I'll probably give a shot at this Legacy myself once I get the Bearers of the Eternal Voice done. It shouldn't be that hard, since I received major help on 1e Legacies a while ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:49:04-08:00","id":1058244,"title":"","content":"The fate is to test and evaluate if they are following their Dharma and the Death is to punish those that step out of their Dharma. Rotting Flesh is a lower level attainment that isn't enough to kill but to set them back on track and the withering is for those that are irredeemable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:51:50-08:00","id":1058245,"title":"","content":"Rotting Flesh is plenty for killing, it just would take more than one use. Not to nitpick the idea, but it does seem kind of redundant to have that and Withering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T04:00:39-08:00","id":1058350,"title":"","content":"I've noticed several things:<br /> <br /> 1. Most of your Attainments shouldn't really have a Duration, not even one that lasts for several Turns. No matter what the tables say, &quot;Serendipity&quot; or &quot;Withering&quot; simply apply their effect all at once. They don't repeat themselves and there is no cool-down period. Only &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot;, &quot;Sworn Oaths&quot; and &quot;Shared Fate&quot; should have a Duration.<br /> <br /> 2. Speaking of those three Spells. How did you calculate their Duration? &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot; and &quot;Shared Fate&quot; are Potency Primary, so they should last a Scene, but could be extended with Spell Factors up to a week. &quot;Sworn Oaths&quot; is Duration Primary, so it's length should depend on your Arcanum rating.<br /> <br /> 3. Also, I didn't realize this earlier, but with &quot;Potency = 1&quot; &quot;Sworn Oaths&quot; is only good for blessings. If you apply Spell Factors you can raise Potency up to 3, but its use is still limited to the weak-willed.<br /> <br /> 4. You've left an empty slot for the first Death Attainment.<br /> <br /> 5. &quot;Withering&quot; does Aggravated damage, so it requires Mana with each casting.<br /> <br /> 6. &quot;Devouring the Slain&quot; makes other attack spells more redundant. Also, it's unusually predatory for the Legacy's beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 03-05-2017, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T05:07:30-08:00","id":1058365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058350#post1058350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed several things:<br /> <br /> 1. Most of your Attainments shouldn't really have a Duration, not even one that lasts for several Turns. No matter what the tables say, &quot;Serendipity&quot; or &quot;Withering&quot; simply apply their effect all at once. They don't repeat themselves and there is no cool-down period. Only &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot;, &quot;Sworn Oaths&quot; and &quot;Shared Fate&quot; should have a Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The multiple turns thing is just my calculation of what it could be the final write-up doesn't have the multiple turns in it. I usually write down what the max of everything can be and then clean it up in editing. Sorry if this confused the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058350#post1058350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Speaking of those three Spells. How did you calculate their Duration? &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot; and &quot;Shared Fate&quot; are Potency Primary, so they should last a Scene, but could be extended with Spell Factors up to a week. &quot;Sworn Oaths&quot; is Duration Primary, so it's length should depend on your Arcanum rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shared Fate and Speak with the Dead are the only Duration spell that is in the Legacy so far and that may change as I do the final write-up. As for the Duration of the Exceptional luck since it has a Fate Requirement of 3 it can accrue a dice penalty of up to -3 or 1 step. Advanced duration take that to 1 scene and the +1 step takes that to 1 day. The Duration of the Shared Fate since it has a Fate Requirement of 5 it can accrue a dice penalty of up to -5 or 2 steps. Advanced duration take that to 1 scene and the +2 steps takes that to 1 week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058350#post1058350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Also, I didn't realize this earlier, but with &quot;Potency = 1&quot; &quot;Sworn Oaths&quot; is only good for blessings. If you apply Spell Factors you can raise Potency up to 3, but its use is still limited to the weak-willed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting that it can only do blessings. You either get a Boon for following the Oath of a Hex for braking the Oath, there is nothing in the spell description that states the severity of the boon or hex or that mentions Potency at all. See Spell Below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058350#post1058350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. You've left an empty slot for the first Death Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have filled that in the Final Write-up by moving Soul Marks to the first attainment and Speak with the Dead to the second attainment, Thematically I like the curse idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058350#post1058350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. &quot;Withering&quot; does Aggravated damage, so it requires Mana with each casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I added that in the Final Write-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058350#post1058350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. &quot;Devouring the Slain&quot; makes other attack spells more redundant. Also, it's unusually predatory for the Legacy's beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am still thinking about this attainment and it is what is holding me up from posting the next draft of the legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sworn Oaths (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Occult, Politics<br /> The mage can witness a sworn oath and ensure that Fate itself enforces the subject\u2019s adherence to her vow. The subject makes a promise and states the consequences for herself if she violates the agreement. No one can be forced to take such an oath, although a subject may be placed under oath unwittingly if he voluntarily makes a vow and verbally agrees to a specified consequence, even if he doesn\u2019t realize the mage can enforce the oath supernaturally.<br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:blue\">So long as the subject adheres to the oath she receives a boon (see p. 134).</span></b></i> If a supernatural power would force the subject to violate her oath \u2014 either by action or inaction \u2014 the mage may make a Clash of Wills against the effect. <span style=\"color:blue\"><i><b>If the subject breaks the oath (whether intentionally or not), she suffers the hex (see p. 134) she agreed to at the time she took the oath.</b></i></span> A subject who declares \u201cI will guard your secrets or may I be struck blind,\u201d will suffer the Blinded Tilt for the remaining Duration of the spell if he fails to guard those secrets, for example. Once the subject has broken an oath, further violations of its terms do not levy additional hexes.<br /> If cast on multiple subjects, each subject may swear his own oath; this is often used to create contracts between two or more parties.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> As long as she maintains spell control, the mage is aware whether the spell remains a boon or has shifted to being a hex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-05-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:05:06-08:00","id":1058389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058365#post1058365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The multiple turns thing is just my calculation of what it could be the final write-up doesn't have the multiple turns in it. I usually write down what the max of everything can be and then clean it up in editing. Sorry if this confused the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all clear now. Well... it will be. Well... it is now clear that it will be clear not now but in the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058365#post1058365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shared Fate and Speak with the Dead are the only Duration spell that is in the Legacy so far and that may change as I do the final write-up. As for the Duration of the Exceptional luck since it has a Fate Requirement of 3 it can accrue a dice penalty of up to -3 or 1 step. Advanced duration take that to 1 scene and the +1 step takes that to 1 day. The Duration of the Shared Fate since it has a Fate Requirement of 5 it can accrue a dice penalty of up to -5 or 2 steps. Advanced duration take that to 1 scene and the +2 steps takes that to 1 week.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've re-read the rules and I'm pretty sure Spell Factors are increased with your Arcana proficiency, just like the Primary Factor is. That's why when you have Fate \u2022\u2022 you can make 1 step for <i>any</i> Attainment, and with Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you can make 2. Can anyone else chip in on the matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058365#post1058365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting that it can only do blessings. You either get a Boon for following the Oath of a Hex for braking the Oath, there is nothing in the spell description that states the severity of the boon or hex or that mentions Potency at all. See Spell Below.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, my mistake. I was under the impression &quot;Sworn Oaths&quot; has a Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058365#post1058365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have filled that in the Final Write-up by moving Soul Marks to the first attainment and Speak with the Dead to the second attainment, Thematically I like the curse idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058365#post1058365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still thinking about this attainment and it is what is holding me up from posting the next draft of the legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>For your consideration, if you decide to keep only one attack Spell <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> had a great idea of using &quot;Empty Presence&quot; as the final Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:21:47-08:00","id":1058391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058389#post1058389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've re-read the rules and I'm pretty sure Spell Factors are increased with your Arcana proficiency, just like the Primary Factor is. That's why when you have Fate \u2022\u2022 you can make 1 step for <i>any</i> Attainment, and with Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you can make 2. Can anyone else chip in on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the passage from the book<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M:tAw pg. 198</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) up to the <i><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</span></b></i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So if I am reading that correctly it goes off the prerequisite and not you actual Arcane Rating. I could be incorrect as I can see where it is just saying whichever is the lowers perquisite Arcanum, but is still at that Arcanums Rating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-05-2017, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:35:53-08:00","id":1058397,"title":"","content":"Also I was thinking of only one damaging Attainment and debating on the Rotting Flesh as a level 4, lethal damage, with a duration of 3 rounds, that would mean with one touch they would take 3 rounds of lethal damage. At level 3 death spell be Soul Armor to protect the souls of your charges and at level 5 do the Empty Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:40:48-08:00","id":1058399,"title":"","content":"My reading is based on this example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M:tAw pg. 198</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment. Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes. If the Attainment also harnessed Spirit and the mage possessed three dots in that Arcanum, the Duration would decrease to two turns, since the secondary factor uses the lower of the two ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text doesn't specify the level of the Attainment, merely caster's Arcanum rating. That's why I assumed it applied to all of them. In this context &quot;Attainment's lowest prerequisite Arcanum&quot; refers to Spirit, because it's lower than Forces. Spirit <i>\u2022\u2022\u2022</i> allows for 1 step to increase Duration. If the Mage in question had Spirit <i>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i>, they could have made 2 steps. The text you quoted can be read two ways, but I <i>think</i> if your interpretation were correct, the text would have said &quot;Attainment's lowest prerequisite Arcanum <u>rating</u>&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058397#post1058397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) that would mean with one touch they would take 3 rounds of lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good ideas, but I think this bit just isn't correct. I you want, we could post a link on FAQ thread and have people resolve this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 03-05-2017, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:50:21-08:00","id":1058400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057671-help-with-custom-legacy-built-around-the-three-fates?p=1058399#post1058399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good ideas, but I think this bit just isn't correct. I you want, we could post a link on FAQ thread and have people resolve this.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need after rereading this it is clear that you are correct, it would only do additional damage if it lasted long enough to reach another interval of my Gnosis-based ritual casting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:55:07-08:00","id":1058404,"title":"","content":"What about the Spell Factors? Do we look for a third opinion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:45:21-08:00","id":1058827,"title":"","content":"I have updated the OP with the current write-up of the Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:40:11-08:00","id":1059125,"title":"","content":"I'm baaack! Seriously, you're probably sick of me at this point. I'll just share my thoughts on your update in case you're not. Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> is making their version of Legacy, so it will be fun to compare them.<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Interconnections (Fate \u2022)<br /> It's neat how you switched out a basic effect with an advanced one, while maintaining their balance. I'm surprised you didn't keep it as a second Attainment, though. By taking the +2R Special effect, you could have measured how the target affected the world - a complete karma scan. I'm pretty sure this Attainment slot should be taken by Serendipity (see below). Most Mages get their first and second Attainments at the same time, so it's not like you'd be losing out.<br /> <br /> Soul Marks (Death \u2022)<br /> OK.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Serendipity (Fate \u2022)<br /> Serendipity doesn't need Advanced Duration. It's a Spell that gives you data. If you need new data, you cast it again. You don't even need to cast it at a target - you just ask Destiny itself. I think you should swap it with Interconnections.<br /> <br /> Speak with the Dead (Death \u2022)<br /> The base Spell is something a Thread Cutter casts at themselves. The Attainment has an offensive effect, so it should probably be Withstood (Composure?). Since it's essentially a different spell, I would make it Potency Primary and boost duration with Spell Factors. It would last a day with Death \u2022\u2022 and a week with Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. You might also want to limit the number of effects running at the same time to you Death rating. Imagine a Thread Cutter walking down the street poking people: &quot;You're haunted and you're haunted! All of you over here are haunted too!&quot; &quot;How long will we be haunted?&quot; &quot;Seeeven daaays~~~&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Exceptional Luck (Fate \u2022\u2022)<br /> OK. Although, does the Attainment not allow the use of Tilts and Conditions?<br /> <br /> Soul Armor (Death \u2022\u2022)<br /> Similar issue as Speak with the Dead. The Thread Cutter could protect thousands of people at once.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Sworn Oaths (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Similar issue as Speak with the Dead and Soul Armor. Also, with Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 you can make two steps in Spell Factor tables. One step in Scale gives you two targets. Two steps in Scale give you four targets. No need to additionally limit it.<br /> <br /> Withering (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> OK.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment</b><br /> <br /> Shared Fate (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Similar issue as Speak with the Dead, Soul Armor and Sworn Oaths.<br /> <br /> Empty Presence (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> This Spell has Duration as a Primary Factor. Its Potency is 1 (3 with Spell Factors), which means everyone can Withstand it (with Spell Factors it doesn't work on people with Composure 3+, which could be cool). Also, you made it last a year, so you probably wanted to give it Advanced Duration, instead of Instant Casting. If you switched the Primary Factor to Potency, the Spell would last as long as your other Attainments and could affect all normal human beings. In theory that would take 1 Reach, but you can waive it as a Legacy boon. If that's too much, make it work only when Interconnections or Serendipity say it should. Also, limit the number of effects you can have running, or you could make a small village disappear.<br /> <br /> It took me until this point to realize Thread Cutters can't benefit from their Attainments. That's pretty cool. It means they consider messing with Fate an abuse of authority. Still, maybe you could let them use other Death Attainments on themselves. Communicating with Ghosts and protecting one's Soul are reasonable things for a Thread Cutter to want.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the 1st Ed Thread Cutters were associated with Moros. They're preoccupied with endings, after all. This meant they got Fate as an extra Ruling Arcanum. It's one kind of luck Acanthus don't have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 03-06-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:43:54-08:00","id":1059172,"title":"","content":"All good observations and I agree with the limit the number of each affect that you can have going at one time. I will think of the number that I would allow if i were to allow them into a game I was running. And never sick of hearing from you I asked for help and I appreciate everyone's help. I realize that in the 1e book they are Moros but I felt that they work better as Acanthus, so I will probably leave them as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}